[quote="Foote"]

At the risk of being the nay sayer...there might be some heros who don&#39;t ever get promo variants. Just like there might be heros who don&#39;t get a stand alone nemesis (Bunker jumps to mind. Frighttrain seems a pretty definitive arch rival, even though his only game presence is in the V5). It might sound rediculous, but it is a real possibility. If it doesn&#39;t fit into the larger story, theres no reason for a promo for promos sake.Omnitron-X is honestly the least likely to recieve a promo of all the heros released. Why? Because I don&#39;t see him being in the overall story long enough or consistently enough to go through any <em>major</em> character changes (which promos tend to represent). From what we definitly know about the story, he gets blown to pieces early during Omnitron 1, comes back sporadically now and again due to time-travel shenanigans, but meets his ultimate fate at the hands of Omnitron-IV (as shown by the Tactics comics and his incap art).Chrono is very likely to undergo some character development. We saw art teased of a Plauge Rat looking very different with the WotC pics from that email sent out, and if that story is continuing in some fashion, you can bet Chrono&#39;s will as well.

[/quote]
<br />&nbsp;

What if Omnitron X has a backup drive somewhere? &nbsp;It seems entirely within the bounds of possibility that it stashed a backup copy of itself, should something go wrong. &nbsp;

I still maintain that Chrono could BE Plague Rat, stuck in a time loop (despite this creating inconsistencies with the bio). &nbsp;&nbsp;

